**1. Modify the existing [Home](file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs#30-69) (GET) method:** 
We will catch the URL payload (`UserName`, `Token`, `timestamp`) inside the existing GET request handler. Upon successful validation, it will perform the login sequence right there and redirect in the same way as the POST method. If no payload is present or validation fails, it proceeds as normal.

```csharp
public ActionResult Home(string UserName, string Token, string timestamp)
{
    // 1. Is it a Seamless Login Payload?
    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(UserName) && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(Token) && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(timestamp))
    {
        // 2. Validate Token and Timestamp
        if (IsValidPayload(UserName, Token, timestamp)) 
        {
            // 3. Mock Modal
            LoginRepository Modal = new LoginRepository();
            Modal.UserName = UserName;
            Modal.UserType = "S";  // Needs clarification

            // 4. Authenticate
            Modal = Modal.isValidUser(Modal);

            if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Modal.Roles) && Modal.UserStatus != "Login Failed")
            {
                // 5. Generate Sessions & Auth Cookies (Using existing logic format)
                var roles = Modal.Roles.ToString();
                CustomPrincipalSerializeModel serializeModel = new CustomPrincipalSerializeModel();
                serializeModel.UserId = Modal.UserId;
                serializeModel.UserName = Modal.UserName;
                serializeModel.FirstName = Modal.Firstname;
                serializeModel.roles = Modal.Roles;
                serializeModel.G2GMobileNo = Modal.MobileNo;
                serializeModel.G2gEmailId = Modal.EmailId;
                serializeModel.UserTypeUrl = Modal.UserTypeUrl;
                serializeModel.UserType = Modal.UserType;
                string userData = JsonConvert.SerializeObject(serializeModel);

                // ... (Auth tickets and Cookies exactly as inside the POST method)
                
                return Redirect(Modal.UserTypeUrl);
            }
            else 
            {
                return RedirectToAction("Home", "Login", new { Error = PortalEncryption.EncryptPassword("Direct login failed.") });
            }
        }
        else 
        {
            return RedirectToAction("Home", "Login", new { Error = PortalEncryption.EncryptPassword("Invalid login payload.") });
        }
    }

    // --- EXISTING LOGIC STARTS HERE ---
    if (Session["ADUserinfo"] != null)
    // ...
```

**2. Add the `IsValidPayload` Helper:**
We will add a private helper method, `IsValidPayload`, purely to calculate/validate the Token, ensuring the [Home](file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs#30-69) method doesn't become overly cluttered.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1. Open the application normally using `/Login/Home`. Verify the page continues to load properties.
2. Provide a valid URL parameter string like `/Login/Home?UserName=123&Token=abc&timestamp=123`. The system should authenticate and redirect directly to the dashboard.
3. Use an invalid token in the URL. Ensure the system safely falls back to displaying the Home screen or shows an error message.
